IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `drca-dates`

-- Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988 (Cth) ("DRCA") -- what a member or former
-- member of the Defence Force (or the dependant of one who has died) meets when claiming: whether a claim can still be
-- made (s 14AA), whether the Act covers the service (ss 4AA, 5), whether it is an "injury" (ss 5A, 5B, 6, 7), whether
-- the Commonwealth is liable (s 14), property, medical costs and the treatment bar (ss 15, 16, 144A, 144B), compensation
-- on death (s 17), permanent impairment and non-economic loss (ss 24 to 27), household and attendant care (ss 29, 29A),
-- the acute support package criteria (s 41B), common law and damages (ss 44 to 49), notice and the claim (ss 53, 54,
-- 58) and State compensation (ss 118, 119).
--
-- SEAT: the individual the law is applied to -- the member or former member who suffered the injury, disease or loss,
-- and, on a death, the dependant who claims. Questions are put as that person would ask them. The Military
-- Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission (the "Commission") and the Commonwealth get no seat: their determinations
-- and the judgments the Act hands them are inputs, answered conditionally.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 20, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00265), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1988A00156.txt, with the formulas sidecar
-- C1988A00156.formulas.md (s 27(2), s 49(4)).
--
-- INDEXED AMOUNTS ARE INPUTS. The printed $80,000 (s 24(9)), $15,000 (s 27(2)) and $200 (s 29(1), (3)) are indexed by
-- CPI under s 13; the printed $400,000 and $110 (s 17(3)-(5)) by the Wage Price Index under s 13AA. No index numbers are
-- deposited, so each question asks for the amount in force (enter the printed figure to use it).
--
-- NEGATIVES. JUST FALSE (or a "no" answer) only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING (or "not covered")
-- where it does not answer, tagged NOTHING-kind with the reason (rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05; NOTES.md).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `DRCA -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `s 14AA -- can a claim still be made`

-- s 14AA: "Despite anything else in this Act: (a) a claim may not be made under Part V on or after the date of
-- commencement" (1 July 2026, s 4(1)). Note 1: from that date such claims "will be able to be made under the MRCA".
-- s 54(1): "Compensation is not payable to a person under this Act unless a claim for compensation is made".
DECLARE `New claim answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a claim made before 1 July 2026 is not barred by s 14AA (the rest of Part V still applies)`
    `no: a claim may not be made under this Act on or after 1 July 2026 (s 14AA(a)); claims that could have been made under this Act are now made under the MRCA (Note 1)`

@export Can I make a claim for compensation under the DRCA on this date (ss 14AA, 54(1))?
GIVEN `the day I make the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you give (or gave) the written claim to the Commission, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `New claim answer`
`s 14AA -- can I make a claim on this day` MEANS
    IF `the day I make the claim` AT LEAST `the date of commencement`
    THEN `no: a claim may not be made under this Act on or after 1 July 2026 (s 14AA(a)); claims that could have been made under this Act are now made under the MRCA (Note 1)`
    ELSE `yes: a claim made before 1 July 2026 is not barred by s 14AA (the rest of Part V still applies)`

§§ `ss 4AA, 5 -- does the Act cover my service`

-- s 4AA(1) (an injury that is not an ailment), (2) (an ailment), (3) (property): the Act applies "if ... (b) the
-- employment occurred: (i) on or after the commencement of section 3 of the Commonwealth Employees' Rehabilitation and
-- Compensation Act 1988 (which was 1 December 1988); and (ii) before the MRCA commencement date (which was 1 July 2004),
-- but not before and on or after, the MRCA commencement date" ((3) omits the "but not" words). (5): employment occurred
-- "before, and on or after," that date "whether the employment spanned the commencement date or occurred during
-- separate periods". s 5(1): "employee means a member of the Defence Force".
DECLARE `When my service was` IS ONE OF
    `all before 1 December 1988`
    `on or after 1 December 1988 and all before 1 July 2004`
    `both before and on or after 1 July 2004`
    `all on or after 1 July 2004`

DECLARE `What it is about` IS ONE OF
    `an injury that is not an ailment, or an aggravation of one`
    `an ailment (a disease), or an aggravation of one`
    `loss of or damage to an aid, appliance or artificial limb I used`
    `an injury suffered as an unintended consequence of medical treatment the Commonwealth paid for`

-- s 5(6): the Act "does not apply in relation to service of a member of the Defence Force in respect of which provision
-- for the payment of pension is made by: (a) the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; or (b) the Papua New Guinea (Members
-- of the Forces Benefits) Act 1957", except (7) a veteran who rendered operational service on or after the Military
-- Compensation Act 1994 commenced and whose pension provision is in Part II of the VEA, and (8) service for which
-- pension provision is made by Part IV of the VEA. Which provision covers the service is a borrowed fact.
DECLARE `Pension provision for that service` IS ONE OF
    `none: neither the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 nor the PNG Act provides a pension for that service`
    `VEA Part II, for operational service rendered on or after the Military Compensation Act 1994 commenced`
    `VEA Part IV (members of the Forces or of a Peacekeeping Force)`
    `another provision of the VEA, or the Papua New Guinea (Members of the Forces Benefits) Act 1957`

DECLARE `Coverage answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies (s 4AA)`
    `no: service on or after 1 July 2004 is covered by the MRCA instead (s 4AA(1)-(3), Notes)`
    `no: service both before and on or after 1 July 2004 is excluded for an injury or ailment (s 4AA(1)(b)(ii), (2)(b)(ii), (5))`
    `no: the injury from medical treatment is excluded because s 8 of the CTPA applies to it (s 4AA(4)(c))`
    `no: medical treatment before 1 December 1988 is not within s 4AA(4)(b)`
    `no: the injury from medical treatment was first suffered on or after 1 July 2004 from treatment on or after that date (s 6A(2A)); the MRCA covers it`
    `no: the Act does not apply to service for which the VEA or the PNG Act provides a pension (s 5(6))`
    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources. s 4AA reaches only employment on or after 1 December 1988; earlier
    -- injuries come in, if at all, through Part X (s 124), which turns on the 1912, 1930 and 1971 Acts (not deposited).
    `not covered: service before 1 December 1988 depends on the 1912, 1930 or 1971 Act under Part X (s 124), not encoded`

@export Does the DRCA cover my injury, disease or loss, given when I served (ss 4AA, 5(6)-(8), 6A(2A))?
GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What it is about` @desc What you are claiming for
      `when my service was` IS A `When my service was` @desc When the Defence Force service that caused it took place (for medical treatment: when the treatment was given)
      `pension provision` IS A `Pension provision for that service` @desc Whether the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 or the PNG Act provides a pension for that service, and under which Part
      `I first suffered the treatment injury on or after 1 July 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury from medical treatment: whether you first suffered it on or after 1 July 2004
      `section 8 of the CTPA applies to the treatment injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury from medical treatment: whether section 8 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation (Consequential and Transitional Provisions) Act 2004 applies to it (it moves the injury to the MRCA)
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`ss 4AA, 5 -- does the Act cover it` MEANS
    IF `pension provision` EQUALS `another provision of the VEA, or the Papua New Guinea (Members of the Forces Benefits) Act 1957`
    THEN `no: the Act does not apply to service for which the VEA or the PNG Act provides a pension (s 5(6))`
    ELSE IF `what it is about` EQUALS `an injury suffered as an unintended consequence of medical treatment the Commonwealth paid for`
         THEN `s 4AA(4) -- treatment injury` `when my service was` `I first suffered the treatment injury on or after 1 July 2004` `section 8 of the CTPA applies to the treatment injury`
         ELSE CONSIDER `when my service was`
              WHEN `all before 1 December 1988` THEN `not covered: service before 1 December 1988 depends on the 1912, 1930 or 1971 Act under Part X (s 124), not encoded`
              WHEN `on or after 1 December 1988 and all before 1 July 2004` THEN `yes: the Act applies (s 4AA)`
              WHEN `all on or after 1 July 2004` THEN `no: service on or after 1 July 2004 is covered by the MRCA instead (s 4AA(1)-(3), Notes)`
              WHEN `both before and on or after 1 July 2004` THEN
                  IF `what it is about` EQUALS `loss of or damage to an aid, appliance or artificial limb I used`
                  THEN `yes: the Act applies (s 4AA)`
                  ELSE `no: service both before and on or after 1 July 2004 is excluded for an injury or ailment (s 4AA(1)(b)(ii), (2)(b)(ii), (5))`

-- s 4AA(4): the Act applies, "in accordance with section 6A", to an injury "(a) ... suffered as an unintended
-- consequence of medical treatment received by the employee that was paid for by the Commonwealth; and (b) the
-- treatment was provided on or after ... 1 December 1988; and (c) section 8 of the [CTPA] does not apply". s 6A(2A):
-- s 6A(2) does not apply if the injury "is first suffered ... on or after the MRCA commencement date" and the treatment
-- is provided on or after that date, or both before and on or after it.
GIVEN `when the treatment was` IS A `When my service was`
      `first suffered on or after 1 July 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `CTPA s 8 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`s 4AA(4) -- treatment injury` `when the treatment was` `first suffered on or after 1 July 2004` `CTPA s 8 applies` MEANS
    IF `CTPA s 8 applies`
    THEN `no: the injury from medical treatment is excluded because s 8 of the CTPA applies to it (s 4AA(4)(c))`
    ELSE IF `when the treatment was` EQUALS `all before 1 December 1988`
         THEN `no: medical treatment before 1 December 1988 is not within s 4AA(4)(b)`
         ELSE IF     `first suffered on or after 1 July 2004`
                 AND (NOT (`when the treatment was` EQUALS `on or after 1 December 1988 and all before 1 July 2004`))
              THEN `no: the injury from medical treatment was first suffered on or after 1 July 2004 from treatment on or after that date (s 6A(2A)); the MRCA covers it`
              ELSE `yes: the Act applies (s 4AA)`

§§ `ss 5A, 5B, 6, 7(7) -- is it an "injury"`

-- s 5A(1): "injury means: (a) a disease suffered by an employee; or (b) an injury (other than a disease) ... that is a
-- physical or mental injury arising out of, or in the course of, the employee's employment; or (c) an aggravation of [one]
-- ... that arose out of, or in the course of, that employment; but does not include a disease, injury or aggravation
-- suffered as a result of reasonable administrative action taken in a reasonable manner" ((2): appraisal, counselling,
-- suspension, discipline, a failed promotion or transfer). s 5B: "disease means ... an ailment ... or an aggravation of
-- such an ailment; that was contributed to, to a significant degree, by the employee's employment by the Commonwealth";
-- (3) "significant degree means a degree that is substantially more than material". s 7(7): a disease "shall not be
-- taken to be an injury ... if the employee has at any time ... made a wilful and false representation that he or she
-- did not suffer, or had not previously suffered, from that disease".
DECLARE `What I suffered` IS ONE OF
    `an ailment or disease, or its aggravation, including a psychological condition that developed over time`
    `a physical or mental injury, other than a disease, or an aggravation of one`

-- s 6(1): an injury "shall ... be treated as having so arisen if it was sustained" (a) by work-caused violence, (b) at
-- the place of work or on an ordinary recess, (c) temporarily away doing something associated with the employment or at
-- the Commonwealth's direction or request, (d) travelling for work at its direction or request, (e)-(g) at or travelling
-- to a place of education, a medical certificate, treatment, rehabilitation or an examination, (h), (i) overseas at the
-- Commonwealth's direction in a declared place or class. (1C): "travel between the employee's residence and the
-- employee's usual place of work is taken not to be at the direction or request of the Commonwealth". (3): (1) does not
-- apply at a place or in a recess "if the employee sustained the injury because he or she voluntarily and unreasonably
-- submitted to an abnormal risk of injury".
DECLARE `Where I was hurt` IS ONE OF
    `at my place of work for my service, or on an ordinary break from it`
    `away from my place of work doing something for my service, or at the Commonwealth's direction or request`
    `travelling for my service at the Commonwealth's direction or request`
    `by an act of violence that would not have happened but for my service`
    `at or travelling to a place of education, a medical certificate, treatment, rehabilitation or an examination (s 6(1)(e)-(g))`
    `overseas at the Commonwealth's direction, in a declared place or as one of a declared class (s 6(1)(h), (i))`
    `travelling between home and my usual place of work`
    `somewhere else`

GIVEN `where I was hurt` IS A `Where I was hurt`
      `abnormal risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 -- treated as arising out of or in the course of my service` IF
    CONSIDER `where I was hurt`
    WHEN `travelling between home and my usual place of work` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `at my place of work for my service, or on an ordinary break from it` THEN (NOT `abnormal risk`)
    WHEN `away from my place of work doing something for my service, or at the Commonwealth's direction or request` THEN (NOT `abnormal risk`)
    WHEN `at or travelling to a place of education, a medical certificate, treatment, rehabilitation or an examination (s 6(1)(e)-(g))` THEN (NOT `abnormal risk`)
    WHEN `overseas at the Commonwealth's direction, in a declared place or as one of a declared class (s 6(1)(h), (i))` THEN (NOT `abnormal risk`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Injury answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is an "injury" under s 5A`
    `no: a disease must have been contributed to, to a significant degree (substantially more than material), by my service (s 5B)`
    `no: a disease I wilfully and falsely said I did not have is not an injury (s 7(7))`
    `no: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, my service (ss 5A(1)(b), (c), 6)`
    `no: it resulted from reasonable administrative action taken in a reasonable manner (s 5A(1), (2))`

@export Is what happened to me an "injury" under the DRCA (ss 5A, 5B, 6, 7(7))?
GIVEN `what I suffered` IS A `What I suffered` @desc Whether it is a disease or ailment (including one that developed over time, or its aggravation), or a physical or mental injury other than a disease (or its aggravation)
      `my service contributed to it to a significant degree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether your Defence Force service contributed to it to a significant degree, meaning substantially more than materially (the Commission's judgment; s 7 may presume it)
      `I wilfully and falsely said I did not have the disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether you ever wilfully and falsely told the Defence Force, for your service or proposed service, that you did not have and had not had that disease
      `where I was hurt` IS A `Where I was hurt` @desc For an injury other than a disease: where or how it happened
      `it otherwise arose out of or in the course of my service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury other than a disease: whether it arose out of, or in the course of, your service in some other way
      `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were hurt because you voluntarily and unreasonably exposed yourself to an abnormal risk of injury
      `it resulted from reasonable administrative action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it resulted from reasonable administrative action taken in a reasonable manner, such as a reasonable performance appraisal, counselling, suspension, discipline, or a decision about a promotion or posting
GIVETH AN `Injury answer`
`ss 5A, 5B, 6 -- is it an injury` MEANS
    IF `it resulted from reasonable administrative action`
    THEN `no: it resulted from reasonable administrative action taken in a reasonable manner (s 5A(1), (2))`
    ELSE IF `what I suffered` EQUALS `an ailment or disease, or its aggravation, including a psychological condition that developed over time`
         THEN IF `I wilfully and falsely said I did not have the disease`
              THEN `no: a disease I wilfully and falsely said I did not have is not an injury (s 7(7))`
              ELSE IF `my service contributed to it to a significant degree`
                   THEN `yes: it is an "injury" under s 5A`
                   ELSE `no: a disease must have been contributed to, to a significant degree (substantially more than material), by my service (s 5B)`
         ELSE IF     `s 6 -- treated as arising out of or in the course of my service` `where I was hurt` `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk`
                 OR  `it otherwise arose out of or in the course of my service`
              THEN `yes: it is an "injury" under s 5A`
              ELSE `no: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, my service (ss 5A(1)(b), (c), 6)`

§§ `s 7(8), (9) -- the firefighter presumption`

-- s 7(8): if an employee "(a) suffers a disease mentioned in the following table; and (b) before the disease was
-- sustained, was employed as a firefighter for the qualifying period mentioned for that disease; and (c) was exposed to
-- the hazards of a fire scene during that period; and (d) [for item 13, satisfies the prescribed conditions]; the
-- employment is ... taken to have contributed, to a significant degree, to the contraction of the disease, unless the
-- contrary is established." (9): a firefighter if the relevant authority "is satisfied that firefighting or related
-- duties made up a not insubstantial portion of his or her duties"; periods add up; only firefighting for the
-- Commonwealth counts. (10): (8) does not limit (1) and (2).
DECLARE `Firefighter disease` IS ONE OF
    `primary site brain cancer`
    `primary site bladder cancer`
    `primary site kidney cancer`
    `primary non-Hodgkins lymphoma`
    `primary leukemia`
    `primary site breast cancer`
    `primary site testicular cancer`
    `multiple myeloma`
    `primary site prostate cancer`
    `primary site ureter cancer`
    `primary site colorectal cancer`
    `primary site oesophageal cancer`
    `a cancer of a kind prescribed for the table (item 13)`
    `another disease`

-- The table's qualifying periods, in years. Item 13's period is prescribed (not deposited); another disease has none.
GIVEN d IS A `Firefighter disease`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(8) table -- qualifying years` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `primary site brain cancer` THEN JUST 5
    WHEN `primary leukemia` THEN JUST 5
    WHEN `primary site breast cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `primary site testicular cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `a cancer of a kind prescribed for the table (item 13)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `another disease` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST 15

@export Is my cancer presumed to have been caused by my firefighting service (s 7(8), (9))? TRUE: presumed unless the contrary is established; FALSE: the presumption does not apply (other routes remain, s 7(10)); no answer: a prescribed cancer, whose period and conditions are in regulations not deposited.
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Firefighter disease` @desc The disease you have
      `years I was employed as a Commonwealth firefighter before it` IS A NUMBER @desc The total years, adding all periods, you were employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth before the disease was sustained
      `firefighting was a not insubstantial portion of my duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of your duties (the Commission's judgment)
      `I was exposed to the hazards of a fire scene in that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(8) -- the firefighter presumption applies` MEANS
    IF `the disease` EQUALS `another disease`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (NOT `firefighting was a not insubstantial portion of my duties`) OR (NOT `I was exposed to the hazards of a fire scene in that period`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 7(8) table -- qualifying years` `the disease`
              WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (`years I was employed as a Commonwealth firefighter before it` AT LEAST y)
              -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources (item 13's period and conditions are prescribed, not deposited).
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 14 -- is the Commonwealth liable`

-- s 14(1): "the Commonwealth is liable to pay compensation ... in respect of an injury suffered by an employee if the
-- injury results in death, incapacity for work, or impairment." (2): "not payable in respect of an injury that is
-- intentionally self-inflicted." (3): "not payable in respect of an injury that is caused by the serious and wilful
-- misconduct of the employee but is not intentionally self-inflicted, unless the injury results in death, or serious and
-- permanent impairment." s 4(13): an employee under the influence of alcohol or a drug (other than one prescribed and
-- used as prescribed) "shall be taken to be guilty of serious and wilful misconduct". s 16(2): medical costs whether or
-- not the injury results in death, incapacity or impairment.
DECLARE `Liability answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commonwealth is liable to compensate me for the injury (s 14(1)), and for reasonable medical treatment (s 16)`
    `only medical expenses: the injury has not resulted in death, incapacity for work or impairment (ss 14(1), 16(2))`
    `no: an intentionally self-inflicted injury is not compensated (s 14(2))`
    `no: an injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct is not compensated unless it results in death or serious and permanent impairment (s 14(3))`

@export Is the Commonwealth liable to pay me compensation for my injury (ss 14, 4(13), 16(2))?
GIVEN `it has caused incapacity for work, impairment or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has resulted in incapacity for work, an impairment, or death
      `it was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `it was caused by my serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by your own serious and wilful misconduct; being under the influence of alcohol, or of a drug not prescribed for you (or not used as prescribed), counts as such misconduct (s 4(13))
      `it caused death or serious and permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in death or in a serious and permanent impairment
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`s 14 -- is the Commonwealth liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it was intentionally self-inflicted` THEN `no: an intentionally self-inflicted injury is not compensated (s 14(2))`
        IF `it was caused by my serious and wilful misconduct` AND (NOT `it caused death or serious and permanent impairment`)
            THEN `no: an injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct is not compensated unless it results in death or serious and permanent impairment (s 14(3))`
        IF `it has caused incapacity for work, impairment or death` THEN `yes: the Commonwealth is liable to compensate me for the injury (s 14(1)), and for reasonable medical treatment (s 16)`
        OTHERWISE `only medical expenses: the injury has not resulted in death, incapacity for work or impairment (ss 14(1), 16(2))`

§§ `s 15 -- loss of or damage to an aid, appliance or artificial limb`

-- s 15(1): "If: (a) an employee has an accident arising out of and in the course of his or her employment ...; and (b)
-- the accident does not cause injury to the employee but results in the loss of, or damage to, property used by the
-- employee; the Commonwealth is liable to pay compensation ... equal to the amount of the expenditure reasonably incurred
-- by the employee in the necessary replacement or repair of the property" ((2): with the practitioner's fees for it).
-- (3): "not payable under this section if the loss or damage is attributable to the serious and wilful misconduct".
-- "property used by an employee means an artificial limb or other artificial substitute, or a medical, surgical or
-- other similar aid or appliance" (s 4(1)).
@export How much compensation do I get for my aid, appliance or artificial limb lost or damaged in an accident in my service (s 15)? 0 where s 15 gives nothing.
GIVEN `the accident arose out of and in the course of my service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident arose out of, and in the course of, your Defence Force service
      `the accident also injured me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident also caused you an injury (if so, s 15 does not apply; replacing an aid is then medical treatment under s 16)
      `it was attributable to my serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss or damage was attributable to your serious and wilful misconduct
      `what I reasonably spent replacing or repairing it` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you reasonably spent on the necessary replacement or repair, including a practitioner's fees for a consultation, examination or prescription for it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15 -- compensation for my aid or appliance` MEANS
    IF     `the accident arose out of and in the course of my service`
       AND (NOT `the accident also injured me`)
       AND (NOT `it was attributable to my serious and wilful misconduct`)
    THEN `what I reasonably spent replacing or repairing it`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 16, 144A, 144B -- medical treatment costs`

-- s 16(1): "Where an employee suffers an injury, the Commonwealth is liable to pay, in respect of the cost of medical
-- treatment obtained in relation to the injury (being treatment that it was reasonable for the employee to obtain in the
-- circumstances), compensation of such amount as the Commission determines is appropriate". (4): payable to the
-- employee if the employee paid, otherwise to the person owed. s 144A(1): "The Commission is not liable, under
-- subsection 16(1) ... if the employee is" eligible for treatment under the British Nuclear Tests Act 2006 s 7, the MRCA
-- ss 281, 282, the Treatment Benefits (Special Access) Act 2019 s 7, or the VEA s 53D or s 85(3)-(7A); (2): unless the
-- Commission determines exceptional circumstances. s 144B(5): no s 16(1) compensation if, because of the table in
-- s 144B(3), the employee is entitled or eligible to treatment for the injury under the MRCA or the VEA.
DECLARE `Medical costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commonwealth pays the amount the Commission determines appropriate, to me if I paid, otherwise to the person I owe (s 16(1), (4))`
    `no: the treatment was not reasonable for me to obtain in the circumstances (s 16(1))`
    `no: I am eligible for treatment under another Act listed in s 144A(1), so s 16(1) compensation is not payable`
    `no: my treatment for this injury is provided under the MRCA or the VEA instead (s 144B(5))`

@export Will the Commonwealth pay the cost of my medical treatment for the injury (ss 16, 144A, 144B)?
GIVEN `the treatment was reasonable for me to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reasonable for you to obtain that treatment in the circumstances
      `I am eligible for treatment under an Act listed in s 144A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled or eligible to treatment under MRCA s 281 or 282, VEA s 53D or s 85(3) to (7A), the Treatment Benefits (Special Access) Act 2019 s 7, or the British Nuclear Tests and BCOF Treatment Act 2006 s 7
      `the Commission determined exceptional circumstances under s 144A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has determined in writing that, because of exceptional circumstances, s 144A(1) does not apply to you and this injury
      `my treatment for this injury is provided under the MRCA or VEA by s 144B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under the table in s 144B(3), you are entitled or eligible to treatment for this injury under the MRCA (s 280A) or the VEA (s 85(2A))
GIVETH A `Medical costs answer`
`ss 16, 144A, 144B -- medical costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am eligible for treatment under an Act listed in s 144A(1)` AND (NOT `the Commission determined exceptional circumstances under s 144A(2)`)
            THEN `no: I am eligible for treatment under another Act listed in s 144A(1), so s 16(1) compensation is not payable`
        IF `my treatment for this injury is provided under the MRCA or VEA by s 144B`
            THEN `no: my treatment for this injury is provided under the MRCA or the VEA instead (s 144B(5))`
        IF `the treatment was reasonable for me to obtain`
            THEN `yes: the Commonwealth pays the amount the Commission determines appropriate, to me if I paid, otherwise to the person I owe (s 16(1), (4))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the treatment was not reasonable for me to obtain in the circumstances (s 16(1))`

§§ `ss 4, 17 -- compensation on a death (asked by the dependant)`

-- s 4(1): "dependant, in relation to a deceased employee, means: (a) the spouse, parent, step-parent, father-in-law,
-- mother-in-law, grandparent, child, stepchild, grandchild, sibling or half-sibling of the employee; or (b) a person in
-- relation to whom the employee stood in the position of a parent or who stood in the position of a parent to the
-- employee; being a person who was wholly or partly dependent on the employee at the date of the employee's death."
-- (4(1) "spouse" includes a de facto partner; "dependent means dependent for economic support".) s 4(5): a spouse, or
-- a child who is a prescribed child, who "immediately before the date of an employee's death, lived with the employee"
-- is "taken to be ... wholly dependent". s 4(4): dependence that would have existed but for an incapacity from an injury
-- counts.
DECLARE `My relation to the member` IS ONE OF
    `spouse or de facto partner`
    `child`
    `parent, step-parent, parent-in-law or grandparent`
    `stepchild or grandchild`
    `sibling or half-sibling`
    `someone the member stood in the position of a parent to, or who stood in that position to the member`
    `another relation, or none`

DECLARE `My dependence` IS ONE OF
    `wholly dependent on the member for economic support`
    `partly dependent on the member for economic support`
    `not dependent on the member`

DECLARE `Dependant answer` IS ONE OF
    `a wholly dependent dependant`
    `a partly dependent dependant`
    `not a dependant`

-- s 4(1) "prescribed child means: (a) a person under 16; or (b) a person who: (i) is 16 or more but under 25; (ii) is
-- receiving full-time education ...; and (iii) is not ordinarily in employment or engaged in work on his or her own
-- account."
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `in full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ordinarily working` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- a prescribed child` `age` `in full-time education` `ordinarily working` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 16
    OR  (    `age` AT LEAST 16
         AND `age` LESS THAN 25
         AND `in full-time education`
         AND (NOT `ordinarily working`))

@export Was I a dependant of the member who died, wholly or partly (s 4(1) "dependant", s 4(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my relation` IS A `My relation to the member` @desc How you were related to the member who died
      `my dependence at the date of death` IS A `My dependence` @desc Whether, at the date of the death, you depended on the member for economic support wholly, partly or not at all (count dependence that would have existed but for the member's incapacity from the injury)
      `I lived with the member immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived with the member immediately before the date of the death
      `my age at the death` IS A NUMBER @desc For a child: your age in years at the date of the death
      `I was in full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child of 16 to 24: whether you were receiving full-time education at a school, college, university or other institution
      `I was ordinarily working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child of 16 to 24: whether you were ordinarily in employment or working on your own account
GIVETH A `Dependant answer`
`s 4 -- am I a dependant` MEANS
    IF `my relation` EQUALS `another relation, or none`
    THEN `not a dependant`
    ELSE IF     `I lived with the member immediately before the death`
            AND (    `my relation` EQUALS `spouse or de facto partner`
                 OR  (    `my relation` EQUALS `child`
                      AND `s 4 -- a prescribed child` `my age at the death` `I was in full-time education` `I was ordinarily working`))
         THEN `a wholly dependent dependant`
         ELSE CONSIDER `my dependence at the date of death`
              WHEN `wholly dependent on the member for economic support` THEN `a wholly dependent dependant`
              WHEN `partly dependent on the member for economic support` THEN `a partly dependent dependant`
              WHEN `not dependent on the member` THEN `not a dependant`

-- s 17(2): "if the employee dies without leaving dependants, compensation is not payable in respect of the injury" (but
-- s 16 still applies). (3): if any dependants "were, at the date of the employee's death, wholly dependent", the
-- Commonwealth "is liable to pay compensation ... of $400,000", payable to or as the Commission directs "for the benefit
-- of all of those dependants". (4): if only partly dependent dependants are left, "such amount, not exceeding $400,000,
-- as the Commission determines, having regard to any losses suffered by those dependants as a result of the cessation
-- of the employee's earnings". (8): the Commission determines the shares. The $400,000 is indexed (s 13AA).
DECLARE `Death lump sum` IS ONE OF
    `the full lump sum, for the benefit of all the dependants (s 17(3))` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `an amount the Commission determines for the partly dependent dependants, up to (s 17(4))` HAS `at most` IS A NUMBER
    `no lump sum: the member left no dependants (s 17(2)); medical costs under s 16 remain`

@export What lump sum is payable on the death of the member (s 17(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `a dependant was wholly dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one dependant was wholly dependent on the member at the date of death (a spouse or prescribed child who lived with the member counts as wholly dependent)
      `a dependant was partly dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one dependant was partly dependent on the member at the date of death
      `the s 17(3) amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 17(3) lump sum in force after Wage Price Index indexation, in dollars (enter 400000 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A `Death lump sum`
`s 17 -- the lump sum on the death` MEANS
    IF `a dependant was wholly dependent`
    THEN `the full lump sum, for the benefit of all the dependants (s 17(3))` `the s 17(3) amount in force`
    ELSE IF `a dependant was partly dependent`
         THEN `an amount the Commission determines for the partly dependent dependants, up to (s 17(4))` `the s 17(3) amount in force`
         ELSE `no lump sum: the member left no dependants (s 17(2)); medical costs under s 16 remain`

-- s 17(5): if "(a) a prescribed child was, at the date of the injury or at the date of the employee's death, wholly or
-- mainly dependent on the employee; (b) a prescribed child, being a child of the employee, was born after the employee's
-- death; or (c) a prescribed child would, if the employee had not died, have been wholly or mainly dependent", the
-- Commonwealth "is liable to pay compensation at the rate of $110 a week ... for the benefit of that child". (6): "not
-- payable ... in respect of: (a) any period during which the child is not a prescribed child". $110 is indexed (s 13AA).
@export How much a week is payable for me as a child of the member who died, for this week (s 17(5), (6))? 0 where it is not payable.
GIVEN `I was or would have been wholly or mainly dependent on the member, or was born after the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were wholly or mainly dependent on the member at the date of the injury or of the death, or would have been but for the death, or are the member's child born after the death
      `my age this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years in the week asked about
      `I am in full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving full-time education at a school, college, university or other institution this week
      `I am ordinarily working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are ordinarily in employment or working on your own account this week
      `the s 17(5) weekly amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 17(5) weekly amount in force after Wage Price Index indexation, in dollars (enter 110 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 17(5) -- the weekly amount for a child` MEANS
    IF     `I was or would have been wholly or mainly dependent on the member, or was born after the death`
       AND `s 4 -- a prescribed child` `my age this week` `I am in full-time education` `I am ordinarily working`
    THEN `the s 17(5) weekly amount in force`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 24, 25 -- permanent impairment`

-- s 24(1): "Where an injury to an employee results in a permanent impairment, the Commonwealth is liable to pay
-- compensation". (3), (4): the amount is "the same percentage of the maximum amount as the percentage determined by the
-- Commission under subsection (5)" (the degree under the approved Guide). (7): no amount if the impairment is not a
-- hearing loss and the degree "is less than 10%"; (7A): none for a hearing loss if "the binaural hearing loss ... is less
-- than 5%"; (8): (7) "does not apply to" the loss or loss of use of a finger or toe, or loss of the sense of taste or
-- smell. (9): "the maximum amount is $80,000" (indexed by CPI, s 13).
DECLARE `Kind of impairment` IS ONE OF
    `a hearing loss`
    `the loss, or loss of the use, of a finger or toe, or the loss of the sense of taste or smell`
    `another permanent impairment`

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of impairment`
      `degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24(7), (7A), (8) -- the degree reaches the threshold` `kind` `degree` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `a hearing loss` THEN `degree` AT LEAST 5
    WHEN `another permanent impairment` THEN `degree` AT LEAST 10
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export How much permanent impairment compensation do I get (s 24)? 0 below the threshold.
GIVEN `the kind of impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment` @desc What the permanent impairment is
      `the degree of impairment in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree of permanent impairment the Commission determined under the approved Guide, as a number of percent (for a hearing loss, the binaural hearing loss), e.g. 12 for 12%
      `the s 24(9) maximum in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 24(9) maximum amount in force at the date of assessment after CPI indexation, in dollars (enter 80000 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 24 -- permanent impairment compensation` MEANS
    IF `s 24(7), (7A), (8) -- the degree reaches the threshold` `the kind of impairment` `the degree of impairment in percent`
    THEN `the s 24(9) maximum in force` TIMES `the degree of impairment in percent` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

-- s 25(4): after a final assessment (other than hearing loss), "no further amounts of compensation shall be payable ...
-- in respect of a subsequent increase in the degree of impairment, unless the increase is 10% or more." (5): for a
-- hearing loss, "unless the subsequent increase in the degree of binaural hearing loss is 5% or more". Read as
-- percentage points (finding 6).
@export After my final permanent impairment assessment, does an increase in my impairment get me more compensation (s 25(4), (5))?
GIVEN `it is a hearing loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the impairment is a hearing loss
      `the degree at the final assessment in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree the Commission finally assessed, as a number of percent
      `the degree now in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree now, as a number of percent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(4), (5) -- the increase counts` IF
    IF `it is a hearing loss`
    THEN (`the degree now in percent` MINUS `the degree at the final assessment in percent`) AT LEAST 5
    ELSE (`the degree now in percent` MINUS `the degree at the final assessment in percent`) AT LEAST 10

§§ `s 26 -- payment within 30 days, and interest`

DECLARE `DRCA party` IS ONE OF `the Commonwealth`, `me`
DECLARE `DRCA act` IS ONE OF
    `pay my permanent impairment compensation`
    `pay it with interest from the end of the 30 days`
    `notify the Commission in writing of my claim for damages`
    `notify the Commission in writing of the damages I recovered and their amount`

-- s 26(1): compensation under s 24 or 25 "shall be paid to the employee within 30 days after the date of the
-- assessment". (2): if not, "interest is payable ... in respect of the period commencing on the expiration of the period
-- of 30 days ... and ending on the day on which the amount is paid", at the Minister's rate (not deposited). (4): "This
-- section does not apply if an application for review of the determination ... has been made". Clock: days after the
-- assessment.
-- The period, stated once: the rule, the last day and the days of interest all take it from here.
`s 26(1) -- days to pay` MEANS 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC `DRCA party` `DRCA act`
`s 26 -- the Commonwealth must pay within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Commonwealth`
    MUST   `pay my permanent impairment compensation`
    WITHIN `s 26(1) -- days to pay`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Commonwealth`
        MUST  `pay it with interest from the end of the 30 days`

-- Runs s 26 over when the payment came. A late payment ends in the interest obligation, not FULFILLED.
GIVEN `days after the assessment it was paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- paid in time` `days after the assessment it was paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 26 -- the Commonwealth must pay within 30 days` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the Commonwealth` `pay my permanent impairment compensation` `days after the assessment it was paid`),
                 (WAITUNTIL (`days after the assessment it was paid` PLUS 1))

@export For how many days is interest payable to me on my permanent impairment compensation (s 26)? 0 if it was paid within 30 days after the assessment, or if I applied for review.
GIVEN `the date of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date the Commission assessed the amount of your s 24 or s 25 compensation, ISO 8601
      `the day it was paid, or today if not yet paid` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount was paid to you, or today's date if it has not been paid, ISO 8601
      `I applied for review of the determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for review of the s 24 or s 25 determination (to the Board under the MRCA, see s 62)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 26 -- days of interest` MEANS
    IF `I applied for review of the determination`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `s 26 -- paid in time` (`days from` `the date of the assessment` `the day it was paid, or today if not yet paid`)
         THEN 0
         ELSE (`days from` `the date of the assessment` `the day it was paid, or today if not yet paid`) MINUS `s 26(1) -- days to pay`

@export What is the last day for the Commonwealth to pay my permanent impairment compensation without interest (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date the Commission assessed the amount of your s 24 or s 25 compensation, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`s 26(1) -- the last day to pay` MEANS `the day` `s 26(1) -- days to pay` `days after` `the date of the assessment`

§§ `s 27 -- non-economic loss`

-- s 27(1): where permanent impairment compensation "is payable in respect of the injury under section 24", the
-- Commonwealth "is liable to pay additional compensation ... for any non-economic loss". (2) (formula from the sidecar):
-- ($15,000 × A) + ($15,000 × B), "A is the percentage finally determined ... under section 24 to be the degree of
-- permanent impairment"; "B is the percentage determined ... under the approved Guide to be the degree of non-economic
-- loss". $15,000 indexed by CPI (s 13).
@export How much compensation for non-economic loss (pain and suffering, loss of enjoyment of life) do I get (s 27)? 0 if no permanent impairment compensation is payable under s 24.
GIVEN `the kind of impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment` @desc What the permanent impairment is
      `the final degree of impairment in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc A: the degree of permanent impairment the Commission finally determined under s 24, as a number of percent
      `the degree of non-economic loss in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc B: the degree of non-economic loss the Commission determined under the approved Guide, as a number of percent
      `the s 27(2) amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 27(2) amount in force after CPI indexation, in dollars (enter 15000 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 27 -- non-economic loss compensation` MEANS
    IF `s 24(7), (7A), (8) -- the degree reaches the threshold` `the kind of impairment` `the final degree of impairment in percent`
    THEN     (`the s 27(2) amount in force` TIMES `the final degree of impairment in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)
        PLUS (`the s 27(2) amount in force` TIMES `the degree of non-economic loss in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 29, 29A -- household and attendant care services`

-- s 29(1): for household services reasonably required after an injury "(other than a catastrophic injury)", "such amount
-- per week as the Commission considers reasonable in the circumstances, being not less than 50% of the amount per week
-- paid or payable by the employee for those services nor more than $200". (5): not "in respect of any week within the
-- period of 28 days beginning on the date of the injury unless the Commission determines otherwise ... on the ground of
-- financial hardship or the need to provide for adequate supervision of dependent children". s 29A(1), (3): after a
-- catastrophic injury, "such amount per week as the Commission considers reasonable" (no floor, no cap). $200 indexed.
DECLARE `Household services answer` IS ONE OF
    `a weekly amount the Commission considers reasonable, within (s 29(1))` HAS `at least` IS A NUMBER, `at most` IS A NUMBER
    `nothing for a week within 28 days of the injury, unless the Commission determines otherwise (s 29(5))`
    `a weekly amount the Commission considers reasonable, with no floor or cap (s 29A(1))`
    `nothing: the services are not reasonably required (s 29(1), s 29A(1))`

@export What weekly compensation can I get for household services (cooking, cleaning, laundry, gardening) I obtain because of my injury (ss 29(1), (5), 29A(1))?
GIVEN `the services are reasonably required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably require the household services because of the injury (the Commission's judgment, on what you did before, who lives with you and what they can do)
      `it is a catastrophic injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is a catastrophic injury (the conditions are in the legislative rules)
      `the week begins within 28 days of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the week asked about falls within the 28 days beginning on the date of the injury
      `the Commission determined hardship or child supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission determined that compensation is payable in those 28 days because of financial hardship or the need to supervise dependent children
      `what I pay a week for the services` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week paid or payable by you for the household services
      `the s 29 weekly cap in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 29(1) weekly amount in force after CPI indexation, in dollars (enter 200 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A `Household services answer`
`ss 29, 29A -- household services` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the services are reasonably required`)
    THEN `nothing: the services are not reasonably required (s 29(1), s 29A(1))`
    ELSE IF `it is a catastrophic injury`
         THEN `a weekly amount the Commission considers reasonable, with no floor or cap (s 29A(1))`
         ELSE IF `the week begins within 28 days of the injury` AND (NOT `the Commission determined hardship or child supervision`)
              THEN `nothing for a week within 28 days of the injury, unless the Commission determines otherwise (s 29(5))`
              ELSE `a weekly amount the Commission considers reasonable, within (s 29(1))`
                       (`s 29(1) -- the floor` `what I pay a week for the services` `the s 29 weekly cap in force`)
                       `the s 29 weekly cap in force`

-- The floor is 50% of what is paid, but never above the cap: where half the cost exceeds $200 the two limits cannot both
-- hold, and the cap is read as prevailing (fork F5, finding 4).
GIVEN `cost` IS A NUMBER, `cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29(1) -- the floor` `cost` `cap` MEANS
    IF `cost` TIMES 50% GREATER THAN `cap`
    THEN `cap`
    ELSE `cost` TIMES 50%

-- s 29(3): for attendant care services reasonably required after a non-catastrophic injury, "(a) $200 per week; or (b) an
-- amount per week equal to the amount per week paid or payable by the employee for those services; whichever is less."
-- s 29A(3): after a catastrophic injury, the amount the Commission considers reasonable. No 28-day rule ((5) is for
-- subsection (1) only).
@export What weekly compensation do I get for attendant care services (essential and regular personal care) I obtain because of a non-catastrophic injury (s 29(3))? (After a catastrophic injury, s 29A(3) leaves the amount to the Commission.)
GIVEN `the services are reasonably required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably require the attendant care services because of the injury (the Commission's judgment)
      `what I pay a week for the services` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week paid or payable by you for the attendant care services
      `the s 29 weekly cap in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 29(3) weekly amount in force after CPI indexation, in dollars (enter 200 for the figure printed in the Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29(3) -- attendant care` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the services are reasonably required`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `what I pay a week for the services` LESS THAN `the s 29 weekly cap in force`
         THEN `what I pay a week for the services`
         ELSE `the s 29 weekly cap in force`

§§ `s 41B -- the acute support package (a situation: the member has died, or a relationship has ended)`

-- s 41B(2): the Commission's instrument "must provide that a person is not eligible for an acute support package unless
-- the criteria mentioned in subsection (5), (5A) or (6) are satisfied". (5) the spouse at the death: wholly or partly
-- dependent, under 65, the death no more than 2 years before eligibility is determined, the death resulted from an
-- injury. (5A) a parent or step-parent of the member who died, or of "another person who was the spouse of an employee
-- at any time before the employee's death" (so of the spouse at the death too): the death no more than 2 years
-- before, from an injury, the Commission satisfied the person is parenting the member's child, the child under 18, the
-- Commission satisfied of crisis or risk of crisis. (6) "If the person was the spouse of an employee" (living or dead:
-- s 41B(1)(b) reaches a related person of a deceased employee too): under 65, ceased being the spouse within 12 months
-- or lives with the member's child under 18, the Commission satisfied of crisis or risk of it. s 14AA(b): no instrument may
-- be made on or after 1 July 2026; the instrument (not deposited) may add criteria (s 41B(7)(a)).
DECLARE `My relation for the package` IS ONE OF
    `the member's spouse immediately before the member died`
    `a parent or step-parent of the member who died, or of someone who was the member's spouse at any time before the death`
    `the member's spouse or former spouse, the member living`
    `the member's former spouse, the member having died`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Package answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: I do not meet any of the criteria in s 41B(5), (5A) or (6), so I cannot be eligible (s 41B(2))`
    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources. Meeting the Act's criteria is necessary, not sufficient: the
    -- instrument decides eligibility and may add criteria (s 41B(7)(a)); it is not deposited.
    `the Act does not bar me: I meet the Act's criteria; eligibility then turns on the Commission's instrument (s 41B(2), (7))`

@export Do I meet the Act's minimum criteria for an acute support package (s 41B(2), (5), (5A), (6))?
GIVEN `my relation` IS A `My relation for the package` @desc Who you are in relation to the member
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when your eligibility is determined
      `I was wholly or partly dependent on the member at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the spouse at the death: whether you were wholly or partly dependent on the member at the date of death
      `months since the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Where the member died: the whole months from the death to the day eligibility is determined
      `the death resulted from an injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the member died: whether the death resulted from an injury covered by the Act
      `I am parenting a child of the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a parent or step-parent: whether you are parenting a child of the member who died (the Commission must be satisfied)
      `the member's child is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the member's child concerned (the one you parent, or who lives with you) is under 18 when eligibility is determined
      `the child lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a spouse or former spouse (s 41B(6)): whether a child of the member under 18 lives with you
      `months since I ceased being the spouse` IS A NUMBER @desc For a spouse or former spouse (s 41B(6)): whole months since you ceased being the member's spouse (enter 999 if you are still the spouse)
      `I or the child am in or at risk of crisis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or, for a parent, the child) are experiencing, or at risk of experiencing, crisis (the Commission must be satisfied)
GIVETH A `Package answer`
`s 41B -- the Act's criteria for an acute support package` MEANS
    IF `s 41B -- criteria met` `my relation` `my age` `I was wholly or partly dependent on the member at the death` `months since the death` `the death resulted from an injury` `I am parenting a child of the member` `the member's child is under 18` `the child lives with me` `months since I ceased being the spouse` `I or the child am in or at risk of crisis`
    THEN `the Act does not bar me: I meet the Act's criteria; eligibility then turns on the Commission's instrument (s 41B(2), (7))`
    ELSE `no: I do not meet any of the criteria in s 41B(5), (5A) or (6), so I cannot be eligible (s 41B(2))`

-- "no more than 2 years before" is read as 24 whole months or fewer; "within the previous 12 months" as fewer than 12
-- whole months, or 12 with no part month over (fork F7).
GIVEN `rel` IS A `My relation for the package`, `age` IS A NUMBER, `dependent` IS A BOOLEAN, `since death` IS A NUMBER,
      `from injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `parenting` IS A BOOLEAN, `child under 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `child with me` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `since ceased` IS A NUMBER, `crisis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41B -- criteria met` `rel` `age` `dependent` `since death` `from injury` `parenting` `child under 18` `child with me` `since ceased` `crisis` MEANS
    CONSIDER `rel`
    WHEN `the member's spouse immediately before the member died` THEN
            (`dependent` AND `age` LESS THAN 65 AND `since death` AT MOST 24 AND `from injury`)
        OR  (`age` LESS THAN 65 AND (`since ceased` AT MOST 12 OR (`child with me` AND `child under 18`)) AND `crisis`)
    WHEN `a parent or step-parent of the member who died, or of someone who was the member's spouse at any time before the death` THEN
        `since death` AT MOST 24 AND `from injury` AND `parenting` AND `child under 18` AND `crisis`
    WHEN `the member's spouse or former spouse, the member living` THEN
        `age` LESS THAN 65 AND (`since ceased` AT MOST 12 OR (`child with me` AND `child under 18`)) AND `crisis`
    WHEN `the member's former spouse, the member having died` THEN
        `age` LESS THAN 65 AND (`since ceased` AT MOST 12 OR (`child with me` AND `child under 18`)) AND `crisis`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE

§§ `ss 44, 45 -- suing the Commonwealth for non-economic loss`

-- s 44(1): "Subject to section 45, an action or other proceeding for damages does not lie against the Commonwealth or an
-- employee in respect of ... an injury sustained by an employee in the course of his or her employment". (3): it does
-- not prevent a dependant suing for the death. s 45(1): where compensation is payable under s 24, 25 or 27 and the
-- Commonwealth or another employee would be liable for damages for non-economic loss, "the employee may, at any time
-- before an amount of compensation is paid to the employee under section 24, 25 or 27 in respect of that injury, elect
-- in writing to institute an action". (2)(b): after the election no s 24, 25 or 27 compensation. (3): "irrevocable".
-- (4): "the court shall not award the employee damages of an amount exceeding $110,000 for any non-economic loss" (not
-- an indexed amount: s 13(1) "relevant amount").
DECLARE `Common law answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may elect in writing to sue for non-economic loss; the election is irrevocable, ends my s 24, 25 and 27 compensation, and the court cannot award more than (s 45)` HAS `cap` IS A NUMBER
    `no: an action for damages does not lie against the Commonwealth or another member (s 44(1)); I can no longer elect, because s 24, 25 or 27 compensation has been paid (s 45(1))`
    `no: an action for damages does not lie against the Commonwealth or another member (s 44(1)); s 45 lets me elect only where compensation is payable under s 24, 25 or 27 and the Commonwealth or another member would be liable`
    `yes: as a dependant I may sue for the death; s 44(1) does not prevent it (s 44(3), (4))`

@export Can I sue the Commonwealth or another member for damages for my injury (ss 44, 45)?
GIVEN `I am a dependant suing for the member's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a dependant of a member who died of the injury, suing in respect of the death
      `compensation is payable to me under s 24, 25 or 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether permanent impairment or non-economic loss compensation is payable to you for the injury
      `the Commonwealth or another member would be liable for my non-economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, but for s 44, the Commonwealth or another member would be liable to you in damages for non-economic loss
      `some s 24, 25 or 27 compensation has been paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount of permanent impairment or non-economic loss compensation for that injury has already been paid to you
GIVETH A `Common law answer`
`ss 44, 45 -- can I sue` MEANS
    IF `I am a dependant suing for the member's death`
    THEN `yes: as a dependant I may sue for the death; s 44(1) does not prevent it (s 44(3), (4))`
    ELSE IF (NOT `compensation is payable to me under s 24, 25 or 27`) OR (NOT `the Commonwealth or another member would be liable for my non-economic loss`)
         THEN `no: an action for damages does not lie against the Commonwealth or another member (s 44(1)); s 45 lets me elect only where compensation is payable under s 24, 25 or 27 and the Commonwealth or another member would be liable`
         ELSE IF `some s 24, 25 or 27 compensation has been paid to me`
              THEN `no: an action for damages does not lie against the Commonwealth or another member (s 44(1)); I can no longer elect, because s 24, 25 or 27 compensation has been paid (s 45(1))`
              ELSE `yes: I may elect in writing to sue for non-economic loss; the election is irrevocable, ends my s 24, 25 and 27 compensation, and the court cannot award more than (s 45)` 110000

§§ `ss 46, 47, 48 -- telling the Commission about a damages claim, and repaying (a situation: I claim damages)`

-- s 46(1) (a third party) and s 47(1) (the Commonwealth or another member): where compensation is payable and the
-- employee or dependant "makes a claim ... for the recovery of such damages", "the employee or dependant must, as soon
-- as practicable but in any event not later than 7 days after the day on which he or she first became aware of the
-- claim, notify the Commission in writing of the claim. Penalty: 5 penalty units" (strict liability). Clock: days after
-- the day I became aware. "As soon as practicable" is not tested (fork F8).
-- The periods, stated once: each rule and its last-day question take them from here.
`ss 46(1), 47(1) -- days to notify` MEANS 7
`s 48(2) -- days to notify` MEANS 28

GIVETH A DEONTIC `DRCA party` `DRCA act`
`ss 46, 47 -- I must notify the Commission of my damages claim within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY  `me`
    MUST   `notify the Commission in writing of my claim for damages`
    WITHIN `ss 46(1), 47(1) -- days to notify`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `me` BECAUSE "ss 46(1), 47(1): not notified within 7 days after first becoming aware of the claim; a strict liability offence, 5 penalty units"

-- s 48(2): after recovering damages, "the employee or dependant shall, not later than 28 days after the day on which the
-- damages were recovered, notify the Commission in writing of the recovery of the damages and the amount of the damages.
-- Penalty: 10 penalty units." (strict liability, (2A)); s 10: damages are recovered when paid. Clock: days after recovery.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DRCA party` `DRCA act`
`s 48(2) -- I must notify the Commission of recovered damages within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY  `me`
    MUST   `notify the Commission in writing of the damages I recovered and their amount`
    WITHIN `s 48(2) -- days to notify`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `me` BECAUSE "s 48(2): recovery of damages not notified within 28 days; a strict liability offence, 10 penalty units"

GIVEN `rule` IS A DEONTIC `DRCA party` `DRCA act`, `the act` IS A `DRCA act`, `I did it` IS A BOOLEAN, `at day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`kept` `rule` `the act` `I did it` `at day` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `rule` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `I did it`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `me` `the act` `at day`), (WAITUNTIL (`at day` PLUS 1))
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 1000)

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `late: an offence of strict liability, with a maximum penalty of (penalty units)` HAS `penalty units` IS A NUMBER

@export What is the last day for me to tell the Commission in writing about my claim for damages (ss 46(1), 47(1))?
GIVEN `the day I first became aware of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware of the claim for damages made by you or on your behalf (against a third party, the Commonwealth or another member), ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 46, 47 -- the last day to notify` MEANS `the day` `ss 46(1), 47(1) -- days to notify` `days after` `the day I first became aware of the claim`

@export Did I tell the Commission about my claim for damages in time (ss 46, 47)?
GIVEN `the day I first became aware of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware of the claim for damages, ISO 8601
      `I have notified the Commission in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Commission in writing of the claim
      `the day I notified it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you notified it, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`ss 46, 47 -- notified in time` MEANS
    IF `kept` `ss 46, 47 -- I must notify the Commission of my damages claim within 7 days` `notify the Commission in writing of my claim for damages` `I have notified the Commission in writing` (`days from` `the day I first became aware of the claim` `the day I notified it`)
    THEN `in time`
    ELSE `late: an offence of strict liability, with a maximum penalty of (penalty units)` 5

@export Did I tell the Commission in time that I recovered damages (s 48(2))?
GIVEN `the day the damages were paid to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the damages (or the settlement amount) were paid to you or for your benefit, ISO 8601
      `I have notified the Commission in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Commission in writing of the recovery and the amount
      `the day I notified it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you notified it, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`s 48(2) -- notified in time` MEANS
    IF `kept` `s 48(2) -- I must notify the Commission of recovered damages within 28 days` `notify the Commission in writing of the damages I recovered and their amount` `I have notified the Commission in writing` (`days from` `the day the damages were paid to me` `the day I notified it`)
    THEN `in time`
    ELSE `late: an offence of strict liability, with a maximum penalty of (penalty units)` 10

-- s 48(3): if compensation was paid before the damages were recovered, "the employee or dependant is liable to pay to
-- the Commonwealth an amount equal to: (a) the amount of that compensation; or (b) the amount of the damages; whichever
-- is less." (4A): (3) "does not apply if the damages were recovered in an action for non-economic loss or by way of a
-- settlement of such an action". (6): compensation under s 17(5) is not counted. (7): only the part of the damages that
-- relates to the compensable injury counts, if the person establishes it to the Commission's satisfaction.
@export How much must I repay the Commonwealth after recovering damages (s 48(3), (4A), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `compensation paid to me before the damages, not counting s 17(5) weekly amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of compensation under this Act paid to you or for your benefit for the injury, loss or death before the damages were recovered, leaving out any s 17(5) weekly payments for a child
      `the damages that relate to the compensable injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of damages recovered (all of them, unless you have satisfied the Commission that part did not relate to the injury, loss or damage for which compensation is payable)
      `they were recovered in an action for non-economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damages were recovered in an action for non-economic loss after an election under s 45, or by settling one
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 48(3) -- what I must repay` MEANS
    IF `they were recovered in an action for non-economic loss`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `compensation paid to me before the damages, not counting s 17(5) weekly amounts` LESS THAN `the damages that relate to the compensable injury`
         THEN `compensation paid to me before the damages, not counting s 17(5) weekly amounts`
         ELSE `the damages that relate to the compensable injury`

-- s 48(4): "Compensation is not payable under this Act to the employee in respect of the injury, loss or damage ...
-- after the date on which the damages were recovered". (5): "Subsection (4) does not apply if the damages were
-- recovered: (a) as a result of a claim, or fresh claim, made by the Commission under section 50 ...; (b) as a result of
-- the taking over by the Commission of the conduct of a claim under that section; (c) as a result of an action for
-- non-economic loss; or (d) by way of a settlement of such a claim or of such an action".
@export After I recover damages, can I still be paid compensation under the DRCA for that injury (s 48(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the Commission made or took over the claim under s 50` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damages came from a claim the Commission made, or took over, in your name under s 50 (or a settlement of it)
      `they were recovered in an action for non-economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damages were recovered in an action for non-economic loss after an election under s 45, or by settling one
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48(4), (5) -- compensation continues after damages` IF
    `the Commission made or took over the claim under s 50` OR `they were recovered in an action for non-economic loss`

-- s 49: a "prescribed dependant" (one who has not claimed, or has asked under s 43 not to be paid) who recovers damages
-- for the death must pay the Commonwealth the lesser of (2) the compensation, if the only one, or (3) the prescribed
-- amount AC × (D1 / D2) (formula from the sidecar), and the damages they recovered. (5): AC leaves out s 17(5) amounts
-- and compensation for dependants who cannot recover damages, less amounts repaid under s 48 (an input: the
-- compensation as so adjusted).
@export As a dependant who did not claim compensation but recovered damages for the death, how much must I pay the Commonwealth (s 49)?
GIVEN `the compensation for the death, as adjusted by s 49(5)` IS A NUMBER @desc AC: dollars of compensation payable for the injury that caused the death, leaving out s 17(5) weekly amounts and compensation for dependants who cannot recover damages, and less any amount repaid under s 48
      `the damages I recovered for the death` IS A NUMBER @desc D1: dollars of damages you recovered for the death
      `the damages all prescribed dependants recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc D2: total dollars of damages recovered for the death by all dependants who did not claim compensation (including you)
      `I am the only such dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the only dependant who did not claim compensation (or asked under s 43 not to be paid) and recovered damages
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 49 -- what I must pay` MEANS
    IF `I am the only such dependant`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the compensation for the death, as adjusted by s 49(5)` `the damages I recovered for the death`
    ELSE `the lesser of` (`the compensation for the death, as adjusted by s 49(5)` TIMES (`the damages I recovered for the death` DIVIDED BY `the damages all prescribed dependants recovered`)) `the damages I recovered for the death`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS
    IF x LESS THAN y
    THEN x
    ELSE y

§§ `ss 53, 54, 58 -- notice of the injury, the claim, and requests for information`

-- s 53(1): "This Act does not apply in relation to an injury to an employee unless notice in writing of the injury is
-- given to the relevant authority: (a) as soon as practicable after the employee becomes aware of the injury; or (b) [if
-- the employee dies first] as soon as practicable after the employee's death." (3): a defective or late notice is taken
-- to be given if the authority is not prejudiced, or the failure came from death, absence from Australia, ignorance,
-- mistake "or any other reasonable cause". s 54(2): "(a) a written claim in accordance with the form approved by the
-- Commission ...; and (b) except where the claim is for compensation under section 16 or 17--a certificate by a legally
-- qualified medical practitioner"; (3): without it the claim is "taken not to have been made until such a certificate is
-- given"; (5): "substantial compliance is sufficient". s 14AA: not on or after 1 July 2026. s 53(2): for loss of or
-- damage to property in s 15 circumstances the notice is "of the accident that resulted in the loss or damage", given
-- "as soon as practicable after the employee becomes aware that the accident had resulted in the loss or damage"; (3)
-- excuses it the same way.
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment costs (s 16)`
    `compensation on a death (s 17)`
    `loss of or damage to my aid or other property (s 15)`
    `permanent impairment, non-economic loss, household or attendant care, or another kind`

DECLARE `Claim answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: notice and claim count, and compensation can be determined on the claim (ss 53, 54)`
    `no: the Act does not apply to the injury without written notice given as soon as practicable, or a late notice excused (s 53(1), (3))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to the loss or damage without written notice of the accident given as soon as practicable, or a late notice excused (s 53(2), (3))`
    `no: the claim is taken not to have been made until a medical practitioner's certificate is given (s 54(2)(b), (3))`
    `no: there is no claim in writing substantially in the approved form (s 54(1), (2)(a), (5))`
    `no: a claim may not be made under this Act on or after 1 July 2026 (s 14AA(a))`

@export Have I given notice and made a claim that counts under the DRCA (ss 14AA, 53, 54)?
GIVEN `I gave written notice as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether written notice was given to the Commission as soon as practicable: of the injury, after you became aware of it (s 53(1)); or, for a s 15 claim, of the accident, after you became aware that it had resulted in the loss or damage (s 53(2))
      `a late or defective notice is excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: whether the Commission would not be prejudiced by treating it as enough, or the failure came from a death, absence from Australia, ignorance, a mistake or another reasonable cause
      `I made a written claim substantially in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the Commission a written claim substantially in the approved form
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the written claim (with any certificate needed) was given, ISO 8601
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What the claim is for
      `I gave a medical practitioner's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a certificate from a medical practitioner on the approved form
GIVETH A `Claim answer`
`ss 53, 54 -- have I made a claim that counts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (NOT `I gave written notice as soon as practicable`) AND (NOT `a late or defective notice is excused`)
           AND (`the kind of claim` EQUALS `loss of or damage to my aid or other property (s 15)`)
            THEN `no: the Act does not apply to the loss or damage without written notice of the accident given as soon as practicable, or a late notice excused (s 53(2), (3))`
        IF (NOT `I gave written notice as soon as practicable`) AND (NOT `a late or defective notice is excused`)
            THEN `no: the Act does not apply to the injury without written notice given as soon as practicable, or a late notice excused (s 53(1), (3))`
        IF (NOT `I made a written claim substantially in the approved form`)
            THEN `no: there is no claim in writing substantially in the approved form (s 54(1), (2)(a), (5))`
        IF `the day I made the claim` AT LEAST `the date of commencement`
            THEN `no: a claim may not be made under this Act on or after 1 July 2026 (s 14AA(a))`
        IF     (NOT `I gave a medical practitioner's certificate`)
           AND (NOT (`the kind of claim` EQUALS `medical treatment costs (s 16)`))
           AND (NOT (`the kind of claim` EQUALS `compensation on a death (s 17)`))
            THEN `no: the claim is taken not to have been made until a medical practitioner's certificate is given (s 54(2)(b), (3))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: notice and claim count, and compensation can be determined on the claim (ss 53, 54)`

-- s 58(1): the relevant authority may ask a claimant to give information or a copy of a document "within 28 days after
-- the date of the notice or within such further period (if any) as the relevant authority, on the request of the
-- claimant, allows". (3): if the claimant refuses or fails without reasonable excuse, consideration of the claim may be
-- deferred until it is given.
@export By what day must I give the information or document the Commission asked for about my claim (s 58)?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the Commission's written notice asking for the information or document, ISO 8601
      `further days the Commission allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc Further days the Commission allowed at your request beyond the 28 (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 58 -- the last day to give the information` MEANS
    `the day` (28 PLUS `further days the Commission allowed`) `days after` `the date of the notice`

§§ `ss 118, 119 -- workers' compensation or other compensation under a State law (a situation: I recovered it)`

-- s 118(1): if the employee "recovers State workers' compensation" (under a law of a State, Territory or foreign country
-- relating to workers' compensation, (6)), "compensation is not payable under this Act" for that injury, loss or damage.
-- s 119(2): if State compensation (under a "specified law" declared by the Minister, (7)) is recovered, the compensation
-- payable "is so much (if any) of the compensation under this Act that, but for this section, would be so payable as
-- exceeds the amount of State compensation recovered" ((6): only the part relating to the compensable injury counts).
DECLARE `Other compensation I recovered` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `workers' compensation under a law of a State, Territory or foreign country`
    `compensation under a State or Territory law declared a specified law (not workers' compensation)`

@export After compensation I recovered under a State, Territory or foreign law, how much DRCA compensation is still payable (ss 118(1), 119(2))?
GIVEN `what I recovered` IS A `Other compensation I recovered` @desc Which kind of other compensation you recovered for the same injury, loss or damage
      `the DRCA compensation otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of compensation that would be payable under this Act but for these sections
      `the State compensation I recovered that relates to it` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of the specified-law compensation you recovered (only the part relating to the injury, loss or damage compensable under this Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 118, 119 -- DRCA compensation still payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I recovered`
    WHEN `none` THEN `the DRCA compensation otherwise payable`
    WHEN `workers' compensation under a law of a State, Territory or foreign country` THEN 0
    WHEN `compensation under a State or Territory law declared a specified law (not workers' compensation)` THEN
        IF `the DRCA compensation otherwise payable` GREATER THAN `the State compensation I recovered that relates to it`
        THEN `the DRCA compensation otherwise payable` MINUS `the State compensation I recovered that relates to it`
        ELSE 0
